@Li7ye Was there any documentation, blogpost or anything like that that demonstrated overriding `AuthorizeFilter.OnAuthorizationAsync()`? We might want to update our docs to discourage overriding `AuthorizeFilter.OnAuthorizationAsync()`, but I'm not sure where in our docs we should put this warning.

I took a stab at trying to make this scenario work with #38851, but I don't think we'll take it because it could break other applications with multiple service providers.

As a workaround, you can implement `IFilterFactory.CreateInstance(IServiceProvider serviceProvider)` yourself. For example:

```C#
public class MyMVCFilter : AuthorizeFilter, IFilterFactory
{
    public MyMVCFilter() : base("myPolicy")
    {
    }

    public override Task OnAuthorizationAsync(AuthorizationFilterContext context)
    {
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    IFilterMetadata IFilterFactory.CreateInstance(IServiceProvider serviceProvider)
    {
        return this;
    }
}
```
